div.p:
[A courtier goes out by the back; 
                     Julian
                       retires to the window, and reads the papers through once more.

[The cry spreads in wider and wider circles without; all talk together; 
                     Julian
                       cannot make himself heard for some time.

[He makes a gesture with his hand; 
                     Caesarius
                       and those with him bow low, and go out to the left.

[The Emperor goes out in great wrath, to the left; 
                        Eunapius
                          and his witnesses retire with the watch; the others disperse.
